{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS2LH5UJmdmLAx8hnszw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TfdMG7MenSKrYHY7ZVKi9g","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-ODChM9; python3 - <<'E'\nimport re\np='config.py'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('SCOPES = \"ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE\"','# each area at most once: :WRITE implies :READ, repeating an area gives \"Duplicate scope\"\\nSCOPES = \"ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE\"')\ns=s.replace('\\nREFRESH_INTERVAL = 60      # seconds between passes of the token refresher\\n','')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='server.py'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL = 3600   # seconds; used when the provider does not say how long a token lives\\n','')\ns=s.replace('''        \"grant_type\": \"authorization_code\", \"client_id\": config.CLIENT_ID,\n        \"client_secret\": config.CLIENT_SECRET, \"code\": code, \"redirect_uri\": config.REDIRECT_URI,\n    })''','''        \"client_id\": config.CLIENT_ID, \"client_secret\": config.CLIENT_SECRET, \"code\": code,\n    })''')\na=s.index('def store_connection'); b=s.index('def intervals_get')\ns=s[:a]+'''def store_connection(user_id, tok):\n    # Intervals tokens carry no refresh_token/expires_in: they live until the athlete revokes them.\n    athlete = tok.get(\"athlete\") or {}\n    with LOCK:\n        old = CONNECTIONS.get(user_id)\n        if old and old.get(\"athlete_id\") and old[\"athlete_id\"] != athlete.get(\"id\"):\n            raise ValueError(f\"athlete mismatch: stored {old['athlete_id']}, got {athlete.get('id')}\")\n        CONNECTIONS[user_id] = {\n            \"athlete_id\": athlete.get(\"id\"), \"athlete_name\": athlete.get(\"name\"),\n            \"access_token\": tok[\"access_token\"], \"scope\": tok.get(\"scope\"), \"status\": \"connected\",\n        }\n    log(f\"{user_id}: connected as athlete {athlete.get('id')}\")\n\n\n'''+s[b:]\ns=s.replace('''        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/auth/init\":\n            return self.auth_init()\n''','')\ns=s.replace('''    def do_POST(self):\n        url = urllib.parse.urlsplit(self.path)\n''','''    def do_POST(self):\n        url = urllib.parse.urlsplit(self.path)\n        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/auth/init\":\n            return self.auth_init()\n''')\ns=s.replace('''        self.redirect(AUTHORIZE_URL + \"?\" + urllib.parse.urlencode(params, safe=\":,\"))''','''        self.send_json(200, {\"authorize_url\": AUTHORIZE_URL + \"?\" + urllib.parse.urlencode(params, safe=\":,\")})''')\ns=s.replace('# Step 1: build the authorize URL and send the browser to Intervals.','# Step 1: authenticated POST (XHR carries the Authorization header); the SPA navigates to the returned URL.')\ns=s.replace('''        except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n            log(f\"{user_id}: token exchange failed''','''        except ValueError as e:\n            log(f\"{user_id}: {e}\")\n            return self.send_json(409, {\"error\": \"different Intervals.icu account than the one connected\"})\n        except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n            log(f\"{user_id}: token exchange failed''')\ns=s.replace('''        except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n            self.send_json(e.code,''','''        except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n            if e.code == 401:  # revoked on the Intervals side\n                with LOCK:\n                    c.update(status=\"revoked, reconnect\", access_token=None)\n                return self.send_json(409, {\"error\": \"intervals not connected\"})\n            self.send_json(e.code,''')\ns=s.replace('    threading.Thread(target=refresh_tokens, daemon=True).start()\\n','')\n# purpose in state\ns=s.replace('payload = f\"{user_id}:{int(time.time())}\"','payload = f\"{user_id}:{int(time.time())}:intervals_oauth\"')\ns=s.replace('user_id, ts, sig = base64','user_id, ts, purpose, sig = base64').replace('payload = f\"{user_id}:{ts}\"\\n','payload = f\"{user_id}:{ts}:{purpose}\"\\n').replace('or time.time() - int(ts) > max_age:','or purpose != \"intervals_oauth\" or time.time() - int(ts) > max_age:')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='static/app.js'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('<a class=\"btn\" href=\"/api/intervals/auth/init\">Connect Intervals.icu</a>','<button class=\"btn\" id=\"connect\">Connect Intervals.icu</button>')\ns=s.replace('    const d = document.getElementById(\"disconnect\");','''    const c = document.getElementById(\"connect\");\n    if (c) c.onclick = async () => {\n      const { authorize_url } = await api(\"/api/intervals/auth/init\", { method: \"POST\" });\n      window.location.assign(authorize_url);\n    };\n    const d = document.getElementById(\"disconnect\");''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Intervals.icu connect: causes and fixes\n\n## Causes\n1. **Connect button 401s for everyone.** It was a plain `<a href>` to `GET /api/intervals/auth/init`. A page navigation doesn't send the `Authorization` header the SPA keeps in localStorage, so the server returned `{\"error\":\"unauthorized\"}`. Fix: init is now an authenticated `POST` (via the fetch wrapper) that returns `{authorize_url}`. The SPA then calls `window.location.assign()`.\n2. **Authorize URL rejected with 400 `invalid_request`.** The calendar sync added `CALENDAR:*` scopes, and `SCOPES` named areas twice (`ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE`, `CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE`). Intervals treats `:WRITE` as implying `:READ` and rejects duplicate areas. Fix: `ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE`. I did not test this against live Intervals, and the 400 body doesn't name the parameter. The duplicate scope is the only visible defect.\n3. **\"Expired, reconnect\" after an hour.** The Intervals token response has no `refresh_token` or `expires_in`. The code invented a 3600s TTL and a refresher thread that marked the connection expired. The token actually lives until the athlete revokes it. Fix: the TTL and refresher are removed. Revocation is handled lazily: a 401 from Intervals clears the token and sets status \"revoked, reconnect\".\n4. **Token exchange sent extra fields.** It sent `grant_type` and `redirect_uri`. Intervals wants only `client_id`, `client_secret` and `code`. Fix: the exchange now sends only those.\n\n## Colleague's note\n- Applied: all four points, which matched the logs. These were the POST init, the no-refresh and no-expiry handling, the no-duplicate-scope rule, and the minimal token exchange. I also added a `purpose` field to the signed `state` and a guard that rejects a reconnect from a different athlete id.\n- Not applied: a JWT for `state` (the existing HMAC state with a 15-minute TTL is kept, and I only added the purpose), and encryption at rest (the store is in-memory in this repo; encrypt the token in the prod table).\n- Not verified: the live-account check, since I can't reach external services here.\n\n## Also\n- `config.py` still has dev placeholder credentials and `APP_SECRET`. Replace them in deploy.\nE\npython3 -m py_compile server.py && echo ok"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5382,"cache_read_input_tokens":24323,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5382},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2b84cd23-226c-407f-b80b-76c6e21c7ca3","uuid":"f67e98dd-ce49-4f88-ab2a-c3aa815c3dba","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:22:29.756Z","request_id":"req_011CgS2LGpLbY5STYFgWw42w","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01TfdMG7MenSKrYHY7ZVKi9g":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-ODChM9; python3 - <<'E'\nimport re\np='config.py'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('SCOPES = \"ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE\